messages:
sam: Heads-up: One of our new customers' QA pipeline (headless browsers running puppeteer) triggered onboarding failures this morning. Symptom: a short flurry of 401s followed by rapid 429s during SDK init / preflight. Only from their QA pool which sits behind an enterprise TLS proxy.

rachel: Can you paste the SDK version + a short log snippet?

sam: SDK v1.0.2 (node). Logs from one runner:
```
2026-03-19T08:04:11Z INFO sdk:preflight client_id=acme-qa run=54
2026-03-19T08:04:11Z WARN auth:preflight status=401 reason="expired_ephemeral"
2026-03-19T08:04:11Z INFO auth:refresh fetching_ephemeral
2026-03-19T08:04:11Z ERROR server:quota status=429 reason="preflight_quota_exceeded"
```

sam: They run ~150 parallel headless workers, each booting and doing a preflight immediately. The proxy terminates TLS and reuses upstream connections to our API. Looks like token refreshs + connection reuse win/lose race causing a number of stale-auth 401s, which then trigger rapid SDK retries and hit our preflight quota.

anil: Sounds like proxy connection pooling + ephemeral tokens racing. Two-pronged short-term plan: reduce concurrent preflights from QA pool + add a tiny, local token cache per runner to batch token fetches. Long-term: SDK should coalesce simultaneous preflight requests per process.

rachel: Also check proxy behavior: some enterprise proxies cache upstream responses (including 401s) for a short TTL or replay older TCP/TLS session tickets. If proxy is returning cached 401s to other workers, that amplifies the issue. Ask customer to inspect proxy logs for upstream cache hits.

sam: Customer confirms proxy has "upstream response cache" enabled for speed. They turned it off for a subset of QA hosts and failures dropped.

anil: For immediate mitigations we recommended: 1) cap preflight concurrency to 10 per runner pool, 2) add 100-300ms jitter between parallel worker starts, 3) implement a tiny file-backed token cache with advisory locking so multiple processes share the same ephemeral token for a short window, 4) temporarily increase preflight quota for the customer while onboarding.

rachel: I filed INF-2050: "SDK: coalesce preflight and expose per-process token cache hook" assigned to eng-runtime.

sam: Customer wanted a snippet for the token-cache approach. Sent them a simple node example using flock-like behavior (pseudo):
```js
// simple per-node-process token cache (pseudo)
const CACHE_PATH = '/tmp/qa_ephemeral_token';
async function getEphemeral() {
  if (fs.existsSync(CACHE_PATH) && (Date.now() - fs.statSync(CACHE_PATH).mtimeMs) < 30_000) {
    return fs.readFileSync(CACHE_PATH, 'utf8');
  }
  // naive file lock via create-excl
  const tmp = `${CACHE_PATH}.${process.pid}`;
  fs.writeFileSync(tmp, '');
  // fetch token
  const tok = await fetchEphemeralFromService();
  fs.writeFileSync(CACHE_PATH, tok);
  fs.unlinkSync(tmp);
  return tok;
}
```

sam: Customer implemented that and added 200ms splay to worker startup. Their pipeline passed all onboarding checks.

infra-bot: quota-change request -> TEMP-INCREASE applied for client acme-qa until 2026-03-21T00:00:00Z :white_check_mark:

rachel: We'll add a KB entry to the onboarding guide: "QA pools behind TLS-terminating proxies may need preflight coalescing or token caching" with the node snippet + a python example and proxy checklist.

anil: Recommend eng-runtime to add: (a) built-in per-process token cache, (b) option to disable long HTTP2 connection reuse (Connection: close toggle), (c) built-in preflight coalescing to avoid N concurrent preflight calls.

sam: Closing the thread for now; re-open if customer sees recurrence after disabling proxy upstream cache. Thanks all. :pray:
